From 368c29ac19f138c657504e8d98318f3af57c2153 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BellSoft <info@bell-sw.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 22:24:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vendor data sources: --vendor-url, --vendor-feed,
 --vendor-strict

* Scans that query api.osv.dev also run vulnmatch/osvlocal, restricted to
  the ecosystems the API does not serve (the vendor's JDK and NIK families),
  so standalone vendor runtimes are checked without any configuration.
  Offline scans match everything locally as before.
* --vendor-url <url> (OSV_SCANNER_VENDOR_URL): base location of the
  archives of all vendor products (<url>/<product>/all.zip).
  --vendor-feed "<product>=<url>" (repeatable; OSV_SCANNER_VENDOR_FEED,
  comma-separated): location of one product, wins over --vendor-url.
  Without either, the vendor distributions come from the offline database
  host (--local-db-url) and the standalone runtimes from the module's
  product base URL.
* An unavailable database of a vendor product is a warning - the packages
  of that product were not checked - and the scan continues with an
  unchanged exit code. --vendor-strict (OSV_SCANNER_VENDOR_STRICT) makes it
  fail the scan. Other ecosystems are unchanged: a missing cached offline
  database fails the scan.
